    {
      "name": "Varanasi",
      "country": "India",
      "description": "Varanasi, one of the world's oldest continuously inhabited cities, is the spiritual capital of India. Situated on the banks of the sacred Ganges River, it is a centre of Hindu, Buddhist, and Jain traditions. The famous Ganga Aarti at the ghats, the labyrinthine lanes of the old city, the Kashi Vishwanath Temple, and Sarnath attract millions of pilgrims and travellers.",
      "best_season": "October to March",
      "image_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Varanasi_Dashashwamedh_Ghat.jpg/1280px-Varanasi_Dashashwamedh_Ghat.jpg",
      "avg_daily_cost": 1500.00
    },
    {
      "name": "Ladakh",
      "country": "India",
      "description": "Ladakh, the Land of High Passes, is a remote region in the northernmost part of India, bordering Tibet and Pakistan. Known for its dramatic, arid landscapes, turquoise lakes, Buddhist monasteries, and adventure opportunities, it is one of India's most unique destinations. Pangong Lake, Nubra Valley, and the Hemis Monastery are iconic attractions.",
      "best_season": "June to September",
      "image_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Pangong_Lake.jpg/1280px-Pangong_Lake.jpg",
      "avg_daily_cost": 3500.00
    },
    {
      "name": "Andaman",
      "country": "India",
      "description": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands form an archipelago in the Bay of Bengal, renowned for its pristine white-sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and vibrant coral reefs. Radhanagar Beach on Havelock Island is consistently ranked among Asia's best. The islands offer world-class scuba diving, snorkelling, sea-walking, and a fascinating colonial history at the Cellular Jail.",
      "best_season": "October to May",
